  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Vétérinaires des Îles d'Or is a veterinary company run by Dr Christelle Luong Van Thi. According to the official business directory (read 18/11/2026), the company has existed since 15/02/2007 and its establishment at 263 avenue des Ilaires, active, has been open since 1 April 2022. It treats pets in the area.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic is in the town centre, Résidence Urban Patio, 263 avenue des Ilaires. The Le Lavandou tourist office, read on 18/11/2026, lists it as open all year: Monday to Friday from 9:30am to 12pm and 3pm to 7pm, Saturday from 9:30am to 12pm and 3pm to 5pm, closed on Sunday. The phone number is 04 94 71 19 26. The tourist office specifies that the reception is accessible to self-propelled wheelchairs, with a slope of more than 5% but reasonable, which can help if you come with your dog and a person with reduced mobility.</p>
      <p>The tourist office does not detail how appointments work: call before dropping by, especially in season.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: outside the hours above, the clinic announces no emergency service; plan for another on-call vet if your dog falls ill in the evening or on Sunday.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The clinic is in the town centre of Le Lavandou, near the harbour, so you can walk your dog along the seafront before or after the appointment.</p>
    </div>

